well don't really remember to much about the early game , except that
i started with a ring of Slow digestion so decided to go foodless. 
This was a fairly typical game for me in that i went for a semi
protection racket. I didn't find any early altars but found
unreadable spell books.  I am not a big fan of carrying around
daggers so i decided to screw the racket once i found 6 spell books.  

By this time my starting pet was maxed out and i started to beat the
crap out of popcorn bare handed. As soon as my level started shooting
up i use daggers and force bolt.  My first set of spells were  drain
life, sleep, extra healing,   fireball,  confuse monster,
enchantment,detect monsters, haste self, wizard lock, and healing.
Drain life was a godsend and ditched the daggers at this point. 

Sokobon gave me reflection and i found a BoH lying around somewhere.
Once i have reflection and MR i considered the game won, but in this
case i didn't have poison resistance and my armor was pitiful. I
still was vulnerable. 

I went to mine town and cleared it out of the goodies i wanted.  I
found a magic lamp (or two?) but i only got one wish. I wished for
GreenDSM and acquired poison resistance. Now i knew i would make it.
I acquired some protection but not the full 9 points. 

I don't remember how exactly but i grabbed the luck stone and turned
my pets into something that took out all the denizens of mine town. I
donated some more gold for protection and killed the priest and
converted the altar. I got my luck up and was gifted MB.  I got
crowned when trying to make holy water. That suited me fine since
there was no way i could have gotten those intrinsics otherwise. I
left for the DoD when my god was in good graces. Finger of death
wasn't a bad gift either, even if i couldn't cast it very well  just
yet. 

When my luck was maxed out i wrote genocide which i didn't discover
yet. I genocided all L. I figured these would slow me down the most
with their summoning storms. Not anymore.

I found a throne somewhere and it gave me a free genocide. The only
things i wanted to get rid of where immune to genocide, so i just
used it to get rid of electric eels. If it wasn't for the throne i
wouldn't have wasted a scroll on these critters. I don't consider
them that much of a threat. 

The descent to the castle was quick and easy.  i made a stash on level
ten and blanked two books to make it even faster. I wrote magic
mapping and detect treasure. I then went to get the eye from the
quest. 

At this point i blew my protection on praying when i became weak with
hunger. I thought i had a prayer free but i must of killed too many 
peaceful gremlins at some point. I actually think that i must of used
my prayer and not noticed it because when i went back to an altar to
repair the damage and check my alignment, it was at pious. I am 
pretty sure that my failed prayer was not due to alignment
difficulties. Just don't ask me what i prayed for, because i can't
remember. 

After level porting to mine town and back i went to get eye again. At
this point i had a scare with a air elemental. Since i normally take
my time i would have an AC 0f -30 and Hp of 200 at this stage of the
game, but instead i was running around with -9 and about 100 hp. The
amount of damage an air elemental can dish out surprised the hell out
of me. I tried to zap it twice with a wand of poly but i guess it
resisted. I then tried slow monster but it would just swallow me back
before i could do anything. By the time i figured i had to do
something different i was down to about 20 hitpoints. In desperation
i decided to pray if i could get down to the critical level and
reached into my bag for a wand of teleport. This action knocked me
down to 8 hp and i was able to pray and then zap myself to another
location. 

The rest of the quest was a cake walk and i reached the castle in no
time. There was a priest on the way there and combined with the one
in the valley i got my protection back. 
I used most of the wishes for magic markers and one for a cornuthaum.
In retrospect i should not have bothered. With Mmapping clairvoyance
was unnecessary and if i wanted +7 head gear an elven helm would have
sufficed. I left 2 in the wand for later use. 

Also, i set my stash on lvl 23 (i think) and this is the first game
were i started to name my spellbooks with the time in turns when i
read them. I didn't feel i needed this information on me because if i
ran out of a spell i needed to know i would just lev port back to my
stash. I thought this info would be useful for when i was going to
the endgame. Then i would know which spellbooks to take with me. 


With the eye, Mmapping and detection this was the fastest i ever went
through hell. Also,being able to write any unknown scroll or spell
book saved many turns that would normally be wasted on finding
polyfodder to complete my repertoire.  (not that i ever poly scrolls.
They are too valuable. Any i don't need I blank and write charging.
You can never have to much power. Ever.)

I did hell the usual way for me. I lev ported to the bottom and went
up. Soon i realized that i would need to have a ring of teleport or
the spell teleport away if i was going to collect any goodies in the
mazes. So my last wishes went to yet another magic marker and a ring
of teleport. I soon found the error of my choice when i ported 5
times and became hungry. (doth!) Oh well, at least i could write a
spellbook of teleport away with the wand. 

At this point i was half way through hell. I was getting antsy with
the turn counter so stopped casting detect treasure. I just mapped
the rest of the mazes and went up. 

I don't remember the sanctum anymore, but i don't think i used my
usual trick of curse genociding purple worms and casting charm
monster. With 900 pw, magic missile, finger of death and fireball i
felt i was more than prepared for all these suckers. 

On my way up i used teleport and cursed !oGL to speed up my game. I
think i had to recharge myself once with a ?oC.

Once at my stash i did some alchemy, but only too extra healing
because they were smoky.  I think i got just one wish out of it and
of course it went to a magic marker. I didn't have many spare scrolls
but wanted a back up just in case a spell had to be refreshed.  I
took two blank books, finger of death and magic missile with me. 

With a wizard with this kind of power i had no problems breezing
through the planes. I did do something stupid and looked into a
crystal ball while next to a hostile air elemental, but since i had
280 hp and -48 ac it wasn't that big a deal. I don't remember if i
fingered him, cast slow monster or charmed him but i got rid of the
problem somehow. I made a mental note that using a crystal ball eats
up a few turns. 

I went through all three altars to get the win. By far the most effort
was required by death since i had to magic missile his sorry ass. I
also wasn't too excited at the prospect of losing too many heps so i
danced with him in the big room leading to the altar. I lighted the
area and jumped around until i could get 2 spaces away from him. 
Then i let her rip. He went down after my second shot. 

I did run out of spell points at one point and used another scroll to
recharge myself. It was really a lot of fun alternating between the
finger, magic missile fireball, and teleport away.

The third altar was to the right , and i think pesty was struggling to
get through a mob. I was contemplating giving him a farewell finger
but that would eat up a precious turn. 

crazy, chaotic male elven Wizard


        
